---
output: preproc
---
@startuml
' A legacy procedure called as "!name()" (the standard library does it, see
' adaml_constant) is a plain line, as before Python: the legacy preprocessor
' calls the procedure, and the "!" stays in front of the next line it gives.
' It is not a Python call (no NameError).
' EXPECT (preproc):
' !title A
' !participant B
!procedure mark()
!$marked = "yes"
!endprocedure
!procedure decl($n)
participant $n
!endprocedure
!procedure show($name)
!mark()
title $name
!endprocedure
show(A)
!decl(B)
@enduml
